# Class: <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008272> (polysyndactyly 4)

AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "OMIM:174700") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "Orphanet:93338") Annotation(<http://www.geneontology.org/formats/oboInOwl#hasDbXref> "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4142-7153") <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115> <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0008272> "Preaxial polydactyly characterized by the presence of a thumb showing the mildest degree of duplication, being broad, bifid or with radially deviated distal phalanx, occasional syndactyly of various degrees of third-and-fourth fingers, and duplication of part or all of the first or second toes and syndactyly.")
